From: NimbleZero <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] panel-mipi-dbi-m: TE sync, scan-order transfer, cached buffers, background sending

Run-time switches (module parameters nz_path, nz_native, nz_te, nz_te_delay_us, nz_onemsg),
sysfs attributes nz_stats and nz_dcs on the SPI device.  With all switches at their
defaults (0) the stock update path is used and only its total time is recorded.
The vendor's own TE code stays disabled; this adds a separate implementation that
tolerates a missing or unusable te-gpios.

nz_cached=1 (default 0): picture buffers created afterwards use normally cached memory
instead of write-combined memory (hardware 2026-11-19: reading one frame out of the
write-combined buffer costs 7-9 ms; with cached buffers 0.8-1.2 ms).  Falls back per
buffer if the allocation fails.

nz_async=1 (default 0): with nz_native and nz_te, the update call copies the frame and
returns; a work item waits for TE and sends it.  The next update waits for that work.

Partial updates in scan order (window computed per variant); updates of at least 1/16 of
the screen start on TE.  nz_fbdev_ms sets the deferred-I/O delay of the fbdev emulation
(kernel default 50 ms = 20 updates/s for /dev/fb0 programs).

After five TE waits in a row without a pulse the driver stops waiting (te_given_up in
nz_stats) until the panel is re-initialised.

The image sets the switches in /etc/modprobe.d/nz-panel.conf; the module's own defaults
remain the vendor behaviour.  Hardware results: docs/results/display-kit/.

